  "implementation": [
    "Count real dictionary-entry roles separately from reactor visits. A custom DXF variable must have one membership in a reachable ordinary child dictionary and must name that dictionary as owner. Preserve standard variable-root uniqueness, alias/dangling/direct-NOD refusals and the prior DWG root rule.",
    "Require a single successful named-resource import and modern source version AC1021 or later. Parse each selected current raw body through the owning parser and match schema/value/common metadata before writer creation. Require a unique represented subclass/schema/value slot; unknown payload remains opaque transport.",
    "Freeze typed model, raw groups/lexical spellings and planned output; bind current data address/import generation. Recheck unique typed/raw identities and values through emission/finalization. Capture containing dictionary snapshots even when no XRECORD is present.",
    "Transcode modeled value1 only when changing ASCII/Binary context, then owning-decode the planned output. Preserve exact opaque fields using the existing raw writer and remapper; arbitrary opaque text/codepage semantics are not qualified.",
    "Precharge 64 times the existing raw logical size plus typed logical size before copies/decoding against the named-resource retention allowance. This is bounded logical accounting, not a controlled RSS/performance measurement.",
    "Reserve selected DICTIONARYVAR and SCALE source handles before generated/collision replacement allocation. Actual peer source handle33 previously collided with an allocated dictionary identity. Debug-only duplicate inventory diagnostics retain both record names.",
    "Before publishing, inspect selected actual OBJECTS record names, unique remapped identities and every retained scalar/reference field, plus owning-decoded schema/value. Refuse late source changes or incomplete inspection. No installed headers, new callbacks/pure virtuals or DWG parser layouts are changed; the private adapter layout changes and consumers rebuilding it must recompile."
  ],
  "controls": {
    "counterLine": "Custom DICTIONARYVAR profiles=128; refusals=24; callbacks=40; retries=64; highHandles=4; textProfiles=12; corruptions=26; identityGuards=16",
    "counts": {
      "profiles": 128,
      "preflightRefusals": 24,
      "callbackRefusals": 40,
      "correctedRetries": 64,
      "highHandleProfiles": 4,
      "textProfiles": 12,
      "outputViewCorruptions": 26,
      "identityGuards": 16
    },
    "profiles": "Four revisions AC1021/24/27/32 x two input encodings x two output encodings x direct/nested child x canonical dictionary absent/present x soft/hard membership. Actual root/entry/owner/handle roles, schema/value/opaque field and owning readback are checked.",
    "preflight": "Twelve wrong-owner/body/orphan/root/duplicate/raw/dangling/child-owner/NOD/alias/raw-only/schema divergences per encoding preserve sentinel destinations; restored sources export using the same adapter.",
    "callbacks": "Five mutations (value, owner, dictionary entry, duplicate typed identity replacing a different member, duplicate raw identity replacing a different member) in four real callback phases per encoding. Forty refusals preserve sentinels, followed by forty restored same-adapter exports. Sixteen duplicate identity cases also directly verify the snapshot guard.",
    "outputCorruption": "Twenty-six replayed completed OBJECTS-view field corruptions across ASCII/Binary are refused by the actual selected inspector; corrected views pass. These are in-memory replay controls, not physical filesystem corruption injections.",
    "text": "Literal caret, control character1, literal Unicode-escape-looking text and UTF8 across input/output encodings. Known value1 semantics are checked; opaque tag300 is retained but arbitrary opaque text transcoding is not certified.",
    "compatibility": "The affected cohort covers existing canonical DXF routes, synthetic typed DWG value edits, named-resource budgets, dictionary sources/defaults/effective ownership, raw writer identity, MATERIAL controls, ordinary CLI/installed CLI and 3D consumer probes. These are scoped controls, not native Linux/Windows FreeCAD or a formal ABI/application run."
  },
